.TH CURSORPOP 1 "2026" "cursorpop 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cursorpop \- animate the X11 cursor (shrink on click, grow on shake)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cursorpop
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cursorpop
is a lightweight daemon that animates the mouse pointer in X11 sessions, mimicking
macOS behaviour: the cursor shrinks when a mouse button is pressed and returns with
a bounce on release, and grows momentarily when the mouse is shaken.
.PP
It works with any cursor shape and in any X11 desktop environment. It draws a cursor
sprite in a click-through ARGB window and hides the real cursor only while the effect
lasts; it uses no pointer grabs, so it never interferes with clicks.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Click effect
.TP
.B \-\-no\-press
Disable the click effect.
.TP
.B \-\-press\-scale \fIf\fR
Cursor size while held down (default 0.80).
.TP
.B \-\-press\-delay \fIms\fR
Minimum hold time to trigger the effect; shorter clicks (taps) animate nothing
(default 120).
.TP
.B \-\-press\-duration \fIms\fR
Shrink duration (default 100).
.TP
.B \-\-release\-duration \fIms\fR
Return-with-bounce duration (default 240).
.TP
.B \-\-press\-ease \fIcurve\fR
Easing curve for the shrink (default easeOut).
.TP
.B \-\-release\-ease \fIcurve\fR
Easing curve for the return (default easeOutBack).
.SS Shake effect
.TP
.B \-\-no\-wiggle
Disable the shake effect.
.TP
.B \-\-grow\-scale \fIf\fR
Maximum grow factor (default 2.0).
.TP
.B \-\-grow\-duration \fIms\fR, \-\-grow\-hold \fIms\fR, \-\-grow\-shrink \fIms\fR
Grow, hold and return times.
.TP
.B \-\-wiggle\-window \fIms\fR, \-\-wiggle\-distance \fIpx\fR, \-\-wiggle\-flips \fIn\fR, \-\-wiggle\-velocity \fIpx/ms\fR
Shake detection thresholds.
.SS General
.TP
.B \-\-fps \fIn\fR
Animation frames per second (default 60).
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show the help.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH EASING
Presets: linear, ease, easeIn, easeOut, easeInOut, easeOutCubic, easeInCubic,
easeOutExpo, easeOutBack, easeInOutBack; or a custom curve \fIx1,y1,x2,y2\fR.
.SH LIMITATIONS
X11 only. Requires an active compositor for the overlay transparency.
